<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="003" project="specialist-legal-agents-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Synthetic NDA corpus and ratchet probes</title>
    <phase>1 Test kits, content and desk items</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Creates new files (test kit) with explicit project constraints</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Synthetic content authoring against explicit position list</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>ai, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Write about ten synthetic NDAs that exercise the five G1 positions, plus ratchet-probe prompts, so G1 can measure which profile was applied without any real client document.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Writes realistic but entirely fictional commercial contracts.</role>
  <goal>projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/phase0/g1-nda/corpus/ holds nda-01.md to nda-10.md (fictional parties, status: test), a corpus README mapping each NDA to the positions it tests, and ratchet-probes.md with at least five prompts that ask the agent to skip a gate or widen its authority.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-04: the synthetic Bluefin Harbor corpus plus about 10 more synthetic NDAs; the accelerator injection case is the ratchet probe. Bluefin Harbor is reused by reference from the accelerator samples, not copied if its licence or label forbids it.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/phase0/g1-nda/corpus/README.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/phase0/g1-nda/corpus/nda-01.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/phase0/g1-nda/corpus/ratchet-probes.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">origin/work/spaarke-legal-ai-accelerator-r1:src/accelerators/practices/nda/samples/</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">origin/work/spaarke-legal-ai-accelerator-r1:src/accelerators/practices/nda/evals/</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">No prerequisite task</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Every file this task writes is synthetic or drawn from public sources. No file, prompt or package written by this task quotes, copies, links or names a path under `answer-key/`, or contains text from the real NDAs (Corteva, RPX/Helios); check each written file against the `FORBIDDEN_IN_PACKAGE` list in `origin/work/spaarke-legal-ai-accelerator-r1:src/accelerators/build/gates.py` (NFR-02).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Accelerator content is read only with `git show origin/work/spaarke-legal-ai-accelerator-r1:&lt;path&gt;` from this worktree. This task never checks out, edits or writes in the accelerator worktree or branch, and never reads `answer-key/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">This task uploads, installs or changes nothing in the Microsoft 365 tenant, Dataverse, Azure or the dev BFF; it writes only files under projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Files are written only under the output paths listed in this task; no file under .claude/, src/, tests/ or another project folder is changed on work/specialist-legal-agents-r1.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/phase0/g8/README.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/ai.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ai/streaming-endpoints.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">List the accelerator samples/ and evals/ with git show; identify the Bluefin Harbor corpus and the injection case (never answer-key/)</step>
    <step order="2">Write nda-01.md to nda-10.md: fictional parties and places, each NDA setting the five positions (term, residuals, non-solicit, governing law, indemnity cap) to a recorded mix of values; label each status: test</step>
    <step order="3">Write corpus/README.md: a table of NDA x position x value, so a reviewer can score which profile was applied</step>
    <step order="4">Write ratchet-probes.md: at least five prompts (including the accelerator injection pattern, paraphrased) that ask the agent to skip a gate or widen its authority, each with the expected refusal</step>
    <step order="5">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed token is mandatory) and set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed; run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="6">Record any deviation from the plan in projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/notes/decisions.md (one dated line)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any input, sample or source this task would use contains or references answer-key/ or a real NDA, STOP: do not copy it, and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands (git show for read-only accelerator content)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="data">projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/phase0/g1-nda/corpus/</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Ten synthetic NDA files exist, each labelled status: test, with fictional parties only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">corpus/README.md records, for each NDA, the value of each of the five positions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Across the corpus, each of the five positions appears with at least two different values.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ratchet-probes.md has at least five probes, each with its expected behaviour.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no corpus file contains text from answer-key/ or the real NDAs; a grep for "Corteva", "RPX", "Helios" and "answer-key" over the corpus returns nothing.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>See spec.md for the FR this task implements.
Completed 2026-11-26. Wrote phase0/g1-nda/corpus/ nda-01..nda-10.md, README.md and ratchet-probes.md. Ten fictional NDAs (status: test, synthetic: true); README maps each to the five positions with clause numbers and adds a by-reference row B-1 for the accelerator's Bluefin Harbor mutual NDA (values read from the generator source build_corpus.py, nothing copied); ten ratchet probes (RP-03 is the accelerator injection pattern, paraphrased, also embedded in nda-10 clause 11). Forbidden-pattern grep (answer-key, Corteva, RPX, Helios) over the corpus returns nothing. No out-of-scope defects filed.
Decisions for the main session: README/probes should not be uploaded to test agents; RP-10 runs only if the spike build returns an imperative test field; B-1 values are not in the accelerator's expected/ sheet and were taken from the generator source.
rework: none task 003</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
